@startuml
' OWNER-MVP-2026-11-04 review: MVP core / cross-cutting. Core presentation/application/files or shared authority/recovery invariant remains applicable.
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #486777
skinparam ArrowFontSize 12
skinparam rectangleBackgroundColor #EEF5FA
skinparam rectangleBorderColor #486777
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFF3DA
skinparam noteBorderColor #B59865
skinparam nodesep 35
skinparam ranksep 45
title Contract outcomes — evidence required for a claim
top to bottom direction
rectangle "Identify exact operation / subject / context\nEvaluate current authority and applicable preconditions" as request
rectangle "Denied / invalid\nNo permitted consequential operation\nDo not expose unrelated private information" as deny #FFF3DA
rectangle "Eligible request\nEligibility alone is not completion" as eligible
rectangle "Actual attributable evidence\nAssess only the relevant effect and context" as evidence
rectangle "Confirmed required success\nClaim the matching postcondition\nApply frame to this operation" as success #DFF1EA
rectangle "Definite failure / bounded partial / pending\nReport the specific known disposition\nDo not claim the success postcondition" as other #FFF3DA
rectangle "Unknown or contradictory effect\nDC-O38: reconcile same operation\nNo blind consequential repeat or assumed rollback" as unknown #FFF3DA
request --> deny : prerequisite not satisfied
request --> eligible : applicable prerequisites satisfied
eligible --> evidence : inspect outcome
evidence --> success : required effect established
evidence --> other : bounded evidence of another disposition
evidence --> unknown : required evidence unavailable / inconsistent
legend bottom
Interpretation guide, not a new execution algorithm, stored enum or retry policy.
Read-only operations and admission/cancellation requests have their own bounded success meaning.
endlegend

@enduml
